## Why This Is Asked
Tests that exercise keyboard accessibility demonstrate familiarity with a11y concepts and deterministic testing approaches for beginners.

## Key Concepts
- Keyboard navigation and focus management
- ARIA roles and attributes (role=dialog, aria-label, aria-live)
- Test determinism with seeded localStorage and deterministic delays

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example test outline in Cypress
describe('Keyboard accessibility for notes', () => {
  it('navigates via Tab, opens modal, saves, edits, deletes, and persists', () => {
    // seed
    window.localStorage.setItem('notes', JSON.stringify([
      { id: 1, title: 'Note 1', body: 'Body 1' },
      { id: 2, title: 'Note 2', body: 'Body 2' }
    ]));

    cy.visit('/');

    // Tab through list and verify focus
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus();
    cy.focused().should('have.attr', 'role', 'listitem');

    // Open create modal with keyboard
    cy.get('[data-testid="create-button"]').focus().type('{enter}');
    cy.get('[role="dialog"]').should('be.visible');

    // Create note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-title"]').type('New Note');
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-body"]').type('New Body');
    cy.get('[data-testid="save-button"]').click();

    // Edit existing note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus().type('{enter}');
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-title"]').clear().type('Edited Title');
    cy.get('[data-testid="save-button"]').click();

    // Delete note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus();
    cy.get('[data-testid="delete-button"]').click();

    // Verify persistence after reload
    cy.reload();
    cy.window().then(win => {
      const notes = JSON.parse(win.localStorage.getItem('notes'));
      expect(notes).to.have.length(2);
    });
  });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design realistic E2E checkout scenarios under network stress, locale shifts, and stock race conditions. It validates understanding of deterministic mocks, proper data isolation, and robust failure handling.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end data seeding with deterministic mocks
- Real-time UI updates across viewports
- Locale and region switching with discount persistence
- Race conditions: stock changes during checkout
- Failure handling, rollback mechanisms, and idempotency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright E2E skeleton
test('checkout with promo code', async ({ page }) => {
  await seedTestData({ locale: 'en-US', promo: 'SAVE20' });
  await page.goto('/cart');

  // Apply promo code
  await page.getByLabel('Promo Code').fill('SAVE20');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Apply' }).click();

  // Verify discount applied
  await expect(page.locator('.discount')).toHaveText('-$20.00');
  await expect(page.locator('.total')).toHaveText('$80.00');

  // Mobile viewport
  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 375, height: 812 });
  await expect(page.locator('.total')).toHaveText('$80.00');

  // Switch locale
  await page.getByLabel('Language').selectOption('de-DE');
  await expect(page.locator('.discount')).toHaveText('-€18,00');

  // Checkout with stock race condition
  await page.goto('/checkout');
  await mockInventoryDecrement();
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Pay' }).click();
  await expect(page.locator('.error')).toContainText('insufficient stock');
});
```

